# Build context hygiene. web.Dockerfile does `COPY . .` for its build stage, so
# anything not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon and baked into a layer.
#
# node_modules is the one that matters most. The host's tree is installed for
# win32-x64 with pnpm's symlink layout; copying it into a node:22-alpine build
# would shadow the correct linuxmusl install with binaries that cannot execute
# -- and `sharp` would fail at runtime on the first ink render rather than at
# build time. The image installs its own dependencies; never send these.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Regenerated inside the image, and .next in particular would
# overwrite the standalone tree the build stage produces.
.next
**/.next
.next-verify
**/.next-verify
dist
**/dist
build
out
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. .env must never reach a layer -- an image is not a private place, and
# DATABASE_URL in one is a credential leak that outlives the container.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Local media store (STORAGE_PROVIDER=local).
.media

# Not needed at build or runtime.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
docs
infra/k8s
*.log
coverage
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
